<title>UK: London gold closes facing fresh 4-1/4 year low.</title>
<headline>London gold closes facing fresh 4-1/4 year low.</headline>
<text>
<p>GOLD - Closed at $333.40/$333.90 down 70 cents and probing 4-1/4 year lows established this week. Charts overwhelmingly bearish. Funds sold earlier.</p>
<p>SILVER - Finished unchanged at $4.66/$4.68.</p>
<p>PLATINUM - Ended $16.50 firmer at $440.50/$445.50. No sign of Russian export start up. Half year buying.</p>
<p>PALLADIUM - Closed up $4.00 at $194.00/$199.00.</p>
</text>
